; A number is no truth value: `x as bool` is refused, the comparison is what
; is written. Until 2026-11-10 the cast cut an integer down to its lowest bit
; -- `2 as bool` was false -- at rc 0. Planner.report_bool_cast#.
; xfail: cast of a int to bool

function truth(x: int) returns bool
    x as bool

if truth(2) = false
    print "PASS"
